        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Yemen's Houthis claim missile attack on Israel in expanding conflict Middle East Issued on: 28/03/2026 - 10:53 Iranian-backed Houthi rebels claimed a missile launch toward Israel early Saturday, their first since the war in the Middle East started. The Israeli military said it intercepted the projectile. The attack came as a surprise for Israel as authorities estimated that Houthis would only join in the war if a ceasefire agreement was on the table, FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky said, adding that \"for now it's certainly an expanding conflict\". 'New phenomenon of dangerous rhetoric': World leaders embrace proud disregard for international law 27/03/2026 Middle East ‘Paradox’ for journalists in Lebanon: ‘High press freedom, extremely low safety preparedness' 27/03/2026 Middle East US, Israeli war goals 'not realistic': Regime change in Iran 'can't be achieved' by airstrikes 27/03/2026 Middle East 'They're putting up quite a fight': Hezbollah pushes back against Israel's advancing troops 27/03/2026 Middle East 'Justice necessary': Yazidi survivors deliver harrowing genocide testimony amid int'l indifference 27/03/2026 Middle East Trump again berates NATO for inaction in securing Strait of Hormuz 26/03/2026 Middle East Trump insists Iran is ‘begging to make a deal’ after Tehran dismisses ceasefire plan 26/03/2026 Middle East As 'war of choice' escalates into international crisis, Miller says Trump has 'no strategy' 26/03/2026 Middle East 'Tehran assumes war is behind them: Iran will not capitulate, Trump has it all wrong' 26/03/2026 Middle East"
